✅ Step-by-Step Guide to Build GStreamer with V4L2 H.265 Hardware Decoder

🔧 Step 1: Install dependencies
		sudo apt update
		sudo apt install -y \
		git meson ninja-build build-essential \
		libgstreamer1.0-dev libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev \
		libdrm-dev libva-dev libv4l-dev libx264-dev libx265-dev \
		libomxil-bellagio-dev libglib2.0-dev \
		libjpeg-dev libxv-dev libvpx-dev


📁 Step 2: Set up a build folder

		mkdir -p ~/gstreamer-build
		cd ~/gstreamer-build

📥 Step 3: Clone GStreamer repositories

		git clone https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer.git
		cd gstreamer


⚙️ Step 4: Configure the build (enable V4L2 + H.265 + hardware support)

		meson setup build -Dgpl=enabled -Ddefault_library=static

🔨 Step 5: Compile and install

		ninja -C build
		sudo ninja -C build install
		sudo ldconfig

🧪 Step 6: Verify v4l2h265dec is available

		gst-inspect-1.0 v4l2h265dec


✅ Step 7: Run GStreamer pipeline with H.265 hardware decoding

		gst-launch-1.0 rtspsrc location=rtsp://admin:Algo12345678@192.168.96.41:554/stream1 latency=100 ! \
		rtph265depay ! h265parse ! v4l2h265dec ! videoconvert ! autovideosink



